3 all "Driver Setup" AVR6552_ATTR_DRIVER_SETUP ViString g
  "This attribute indicates the Driver Setup string that the user specified "
  "when initializing the driver.\n"
  "\n"
  "Some cases exist where the end-user must specify instrument driver options "
  "at initialization time.  An example of this is specifying a particular "
  "instrument model from among a family of instruments that the driver "
  "supports.  This is useful when using simulation.  The end-user can specify "
  "driver-specific options through the DriverSetup keyword in the "
  "optionsString parameter to the avr6552_InitWithOptions function, or "
  "through the IVI Configuration Utility.\n"
  "\n"
  "If the user does not specify a Driver Setup string, this attribute returns "
  "an empty string.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1050007"

3 all "Logical Name" AVR6552_ATTR_LOGICAL_NAME ViString g
  "A string containing the logical name you specified when opening the "
  "current IVI session.\n"
  "     You may pass a logical name to the avr6552_init or "
  "avr6552_InitWithOptions functions.  The IVI Configuration utility must "
  "contain an entry for the logical name.  The logical name entry refers to a "
  "virtual instrument section in the IVI Configuration file.  The virtual "
  "instrument section specifies a physical device and initial user options.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1050305"

3 all "Resource Descriptor" AVR6552_ATTR_IO_RESOURCE_DESCRIPTOR ViString g
  "Indicates the resource descriptor the driver uses to identify the "
  "physical device.\n"
  "    If you initialize the driver with a logical name, this attribute "
  "contains the resource descriptor that corresponds to the entry in the IVI "
  "Configuration utility.  \n"
  "    If you initialize the instrument driver with the resource descriptor, "
  "this attribute contains that value.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1050304"

1 all "Basic Operation"
  "Attributes that control the basic features of the DMM."

2 all "Function" AVR6552_ATTR_FUNCTION ViInt32 gs
  "Specifies the measurement function.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250001"

2 all "Range" AVR6552_ATTR_RANGE ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the measurement range.  You use positive values to represent "
  "the absolute value of the maximum expected measurement.  The value is in "
  "units appropriate for the current value of the AVR6552_ATTR_FUNCTION "
  "attribute.  For example, when you set the AVR6552_ATTR_FUNCTION attribute "
  "to AVR6552_VAL_DC_VOLTS, the units are volts.  For example, setting this "
  "attribute to 10.0 configures the DMM to measure DC voltages from -10.0 to "
  "+10.0 volts.\n"
  "    Negative values are reserved for controlling the DMM's auto-ranging "
  "capability.\n"
  "- AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_RANGE_ON (-1.0) - Configures the DMM to calculate the "
  "range before each measurement automatically.\n"
  "    For AVR6552, When you set this attribute to AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_RANGE_ON, "
  "you cannot obtain the actual range the DMM is currently using.\n"
  "\n"
  "Note:  \n"
  "(1)  For frequency or diode measurements, this attribute must be set to "
  "AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_RANGE_ON.    \n"
  "\n"
  "(2) This attribute must be set to  AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_RANGE_ON in burst "
  "measurement mode.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250002"

2 all "Resolution" AVR6552_ATTR_RESOLUTION_ABSOLUTE ViReal64 gs attrResolutionAbsoluteRangeTable
  "This attribute configures the measurement resolution of the DMM in "
  "absolute units.\n"
  "\n"
  "Setting this attribute to lower values increases the measurement accuracy. "
  " Setting this attribute to higher values increases the measurement speed.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250008"

2 all "Digits Resolution" AVR6552_ATTR_RESOLUTION ViReal64 gs
  "This attributes specifies the measurement resolution in digits of "
  "precision.\n"
  "\n"
  "Note:  For AVR6552 series, the allowable resolution value depends on the "
  "sample rates as well as measurement function as following table shows:\n"
  "---------------------------------------------------\n"
  "|    Measurement       |      Sampling Rate       |\n"
  "|     Function         |--------------------------|\n"
  "|                      |   SLOW/MED  |    FAST    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|       DCV            |     5.5     |     4.5    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|     2W/4W Res        |     5.5     |     4.5    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|    LP 2/4W Res       |     5.5     |     4.5    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|        ACV           |     5.5     |     4.5    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|        DCI           |     5.5     |     4.5    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|        ACI           |     5.5     |     4.5    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|      ACV (AC+DC)     |     4.5     |     3.5    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|      ACI (AC+DC)     |     4.5     |     3.5    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|         Diode        |     5.5     |     4.5    |\n"
  "|----------------------|-------------|------------|\n"
  "|        Ripple V      |     3.5     |     3.5    |\n"
  "---------------------------------------------------\n"
  "| Measurement |             Sampling Rate         |\n"
  "| Function    |-----------------------------------| \n"
  "|             |    SLOW   |    MED     |   FAST   |\n"
  "|-------------|-----------|------------|----------|\n"
  "|   FREQ      |    6.0    |     5.0    |    4.0   |\n"
  "--------------------------------------------------- \n"
  "When sample rate is set to long-it, the same number of digits as those of "
  "the MED are displayed.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150028"

1 all "Sample Rate"
  "Attributes for configuring the sample rate"

2 all "Sample Rate" AVR6552_ATTR_SAMPLE_RATE ViInt32 gs
  "Specifies the sample rate the DMM uses to acquire a signal.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150004"

2 all "Integral Time" AVR6552_ATTR_INTEGRAL_TIME ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the integral time for long-it sample rate.  The units for this "
  "attribute are milliseconds.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150005"

1 all "Trigger"
  "Attributes that configure the triggering capabilities of the DMM."

2 all "Trigger Source" AVR6552_ATTR_TRIGGER_SOURCE ViInt32 gs attrTriggerSourceRangeTable
  "This attribute specifies the trigger source.\n"
  " \n"
  "Valid Values:\n"
  "\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_IMMEDIATE - Immediate (Default)\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250004"

2 all "Trigger Delay" AVR6552_ATTR_TRIGGER_DELAY ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the length of time the DMM waits after it receives the trigger "
  "and before it takes a measurement.  Use positive values to set the trigger "
  "delay in seconds. \n"
  "    \n"
  "    Valid Range:  0.0 seconds\n"
  "\n"
  "Note:  This attribute does not affect the behavior of the DMM. It exists "
  "only for class compliance.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250005"

2 all "Trigger Operations"
  "Attributes that configure the measurement flow of the DMM. These include "
  "the sample mode and settings particular to each sample mode.\n"
  "    "

3 all "Sample Mode" AVR6552_ATTR_SAMPLE_MODE ViInt32 gs attrSampleModeRangeTable
  "Specifies the sample mode the DMM to use.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150002"

3 all "Delay" AVR6552_ATTR_DELAY ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the delay the DMM uses for the HOLD and BURST sample modes "
  "before it takes a measurement.\n"
  "\n"
  "Valid Values:  0.0 - 99.999 seconds\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150003"

3 all "Hold Sample Count" AVR6552_ATTR_HOLD_SAMPLE_COUNT ViInt32 gs
  "Specifies the number of measurements the DMM takes each time it receives "
  "a trigger in Hold sample mode.\n"
  "    \n"
  "Valid Values:  1 - 9999\n"
  "\n"
  "Note:  This attribute does not affect the behavior of the instrument if "
  "the  AVR6552_ATTR_SAMPLE_MODE attribute is not set to AVR6552_VAL_HOLD.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150008"

3 all "Burst Count" AVR6552_ATTR_BURST_COUNT ViInt32 gs attrBurstCountRangeTable
  "Specifies the measurement count to transfer to the internal memory in "
  "burst sample mode.\n"
  "\n"
  "Notes:  \n"
  "(1)  This attribute does not affect the behavior of the instrument if the "
  "sample mode is not set to burst mode.\n"
  "(2)  This attribute is supported only by AVR6552.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150006"

3 all "Delayed Trigger" AVR6552_ATTR_DELAYED_TRIGGER ViInt32 gs attrDelayedTriggerRangeTable
  "Specifies the percentage of numbers of premeasurement cycles out of the "
  "total burst cycles.\n"
  "\n"
  "Notes:  \n"
  "(1)  This attribute does not affect the behavior of the instrument if the "
  "sample mode is not set to burst mode.\n"
  "(2)  This attribute is supported only by AVR6552.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150007"

1 all "AC Measurements"
  "Attributes that configure additional parameters for AC voltage or AC "
  "current measurements."

2 all "AC Maximum Frequency" AVR6552_ATTR_AC_MAX_FREQ ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the maximum frequency component of the input signal for AC "
  "measurements. The value of this attribute affects instrument behavior only "
  "when you set the AVR6552_ATTR_FUNCTION attribute to one of the following "
  "values:\n"
  "\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_AC_VOLTS\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_AC_CURRENT\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_AC_PLUS_DC_VOLTS\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_AC_PLUS_DC_CURRENT\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250007"

2 all "AC Minimum Frequency" AVR6552_ATTR_AC_MIN_FREQ ViReal64 gs attrAcMinFreqRangeTable
  "Specifies the minimum frequency component of the input signal for AC "
  "measurements.  The value of this attribute affects instrument behavior "
  "only when you set the AVR6552_ATTR_FUNCTION attribute to one of the "
  "following values:\n"
  "\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_AC_VOLTS\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_AC_CURRENT\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_AC_PLUS_DC_VOLTS\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_AC_PLUS_DC_CURRENT\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250006"

1 all "Frequency Measurements"
  "Attributes that configure additional parameters for frequency "
  "measurements."

2 all "Frequency Voltage Range" AVR6552_ATTR_FREQ_VOLTAGE_RANGE ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the expected maximum value of the input signal for frequency "
  "measurements in volts RMS.\n"
  "\n"
  "Valid Range: 0.1 - 700.0 volts RMS\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250101"

1 all "Ripple Voltage Measurements"
  "Attributes that configure additional parameters for Ripple Volts "
  "measurements."

2 all "Low Pass Filter" AVR6552_ATTR_LOW_PASS_FILTER ViInt32 gs attrLowPassFilterRangeTable
  "Specifies the frequency band of LPF (low-pass filter) the DMM uses to "
  "measure ripple voltage.\n"
  "\n"
  "Note:  This attribute is supported only by AVR6552T-R.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150020"

2 all "High Pass Filter" AVR6552_ATTR_HIGH_PASS_FILTER ViInt32 gs attrHighPassFilterRangeTable
  "Specifies the frequency band of HPF (high-pass filter) the DMM uses to "
  "measure ripple voltage.\n"
  "\n"
  "Note:  This attribute is supported only by AVR6552T-R.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150019"

1 all "Measurement Operation Options"
  "Attributes that configure different measurement options."

2 all "Auto Zero" AVR6552_ATTR_AUTO_ZERO ViInt32 gs attrAutoZeroRangeTable
  "Specifies the auto-zero mode.  In general, the auto-zero capability of a "
  "DMM normalizes all measurements based on a Zero Reading.  When "
  "auto-zeroing is enabled, the DMM internally disconnects the input signal "
  "and takes a Zero Reading.  The DMM then subtracts the Zero Reading from "
  "the measurement.  This prevents offset voltages present in the DMM's input "
  "circuitry from affecting measurement accuracy.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250332"

2 all "Powerline Frequency" AVR6552_ATTR_POWERLINE_FREQ ViReal64 g attrPowerlineFreqRangeTable
  "Specifies the power line frequency in Hertz.\n"
  "    \n"
  "The instrument selects the powerline frequency automatically. This "
  "attribute cannot be set by the user.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1250333"

2 all "Null Calculation"
  "Attributes for configuring null calculation."

3 all "Null Calculation Enabled" AVR6552_ATTR_NULL_ENABLED ViBoolean gs Boolean_values
  "Enable/Disable Null calculation\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150022"

3 all "Null Offset" AVR6552_ATTR_NULL_OFFSET ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the offset for null operation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150011"

2 all "Smoothing Calculation"
  "Attributes for configuring smoothing calculation"

3 all "Smoothing Enabled" AVR6552_ATTR_SMOOTH_ENABLED ViBoolean gs Boolean_values
  "Enable/Disable Smoothing\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150023"

3 all "Smooth Count" AVR6552_ATTR_SMOOTH_COUNT ViInt32 gs
  "Specifies the cycle count for smoothing calculation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150012"

2 all "Comparison Calculation"
  "Attributes for configuring comparison calculation."

3 all "Compare Enabled" AVR6552_ATTR_COMPARE_ENABLED ViBoolean gs Boolean_values
  "Enable/Disable Comparison calculation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150024"

3 all "Compare High Constant Value" AVR6552_ATTR_COMPARE_HIGH_VAL ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the high value for comparison calculation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150013"

3 all "Compare Low Constant Value" AVR6552_ATTR_COMPARE_LOW_VAL ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the low value for comparison calculation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150014"

2 all "Scaling Calculation"
  "Attributes for configuring scaling calculation."

3 all "Scaling Enabled" AVR6552_ATTR_SCALE_ENABLED ViBoolean gs Boolean_values
  "Enable/Disable Scaling\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150025"

3 all "A Value for Scale Operation" AVR6552_ATTR_SCALE_A ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the first constant (constant A) for scale calculation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150015"

3 all "B Value for Scale Operation" AVR6552_ATTR_SCALE_B ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the second constant (constant B) for scale calculation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150016"

3 all "C Value for Scale Operation" AVR6552_ATTR_SCALE_C ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the third constant (constant C) for scale calculation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150017"

2 all "Max-Min Calculation"
  "Attributes for configuring the MaxMin calculation."

3 all "Max Min Enabled" AVR6552_ATTR_MAX_MIN_ENABLED ViBoolean gs Boolean_values
  "Enable/Disable the MaxMin calculation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150026"

2 all "dB/dBm Calculation"
  "Attribute for configuring dB/dBm calculation."

3 all "dB Mode" AVR6552_ATTR_DB_MODE ViInt32 gs avr6552AttrDbModeRangeTable
  "Specifies the decible conversion to perform.\n"
  "\n"
  "Defined Values:\n"
  "\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_DB_OFF - Disable the dB/dBm calculation\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_DB_ON  - Enable the dB calculation\n"
  "AVR6552_VAL_DBM_ON - Enable the dBm calculation\n"
  "\n"
  "Notes:\n"
  "\n"
  "(1) The dB calculation executes a decibel converison. It is functional "
  "only during voltage measurements. \n"
  "\n"
  "(2) The dBm calculation is useful for calculating the power gain  per mV. "
  "It is functional only during voltage measurements.\n"
  "\n"
  "(3) The db, dBm, and scaling calculations cannot be selected at the same "
  "time.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150027"

3 all "DB/DBM Constant" AVR6552_ATTR_DB_CONSTANT ViReal64 gs
  "Specifies the constant for dB and dBm operation.\n"
  "\n"
  "Attribute Value: 1150018"

